If you don't like it, don't use it!!  Just set window:tty in your NetHack
Defaults file, and you've got the old style tty back again. (If you are
still playing 3.0j, I think the consensus is get 3.1.3!  It really should
have been NH 4.0, not 3.1  :-) ).

When I play on a large screen, the Mac windowed interface is far superior
to the tty version (IMHO).  When I play on a small screen (Powerbook), the
tty is better (only one window).

Besides, I don't see where the "pop-up-and-click" interface is _required_
when using Mac windows.  The only time I find it useful to use the mouse at
all in NH is when identifying with /.  First letter identifiers still work,
and a space bar dismisses info popups nicely.



Whats the problem??????


PS - I do admit to prefering the old style num_pad interface, with jkl on
the keyboard for jump kick loot.  You can fix this in NH for Mac with a
ResEdit hack to the NetHAck application file - I will share details if
anybody is interested.


